+# CPU batch-replay backend
+
+This backend replays generation requests through the Language Model Evaluation Harness without fetching weights. Use the normal registry and harness request type:
+
+```python
+from lm_eval.api.instance import Instance
+from lm_eval.api.registry import get_model
+
+backend = get_model("codesense-batch")(model="m1", tenant="local", mode="packed")
+row = Instance("generate_until", {}, ("parity", {"max_gen_toks": 4}), idx=0)
+result = backend.generate_until([row])
+```
+
+Text is encoded as UTF-8 bytes. Each returned token selects a character from
+`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz01234` at its integer value modulo 31. A string
+or list of strings in `until` ends the returned text at the earliest matching
+position, excluding the marker. Empty markers are ignored. The adapter accepts
+`max_gen_toks` (default 4), `temperature` (default 0), `min_new_tokens`,
+`eos_token_id`, `context_length`, `seed` and `shard`. Generation is
+deterministic. Scoring likelihoods and stochastic sampling are unsupported.
+
+Choose a serving model, tenant, adapter and deployment revision when creating
+the backend. Each of these identifies an experiment; the caller updates its
+revision when deploying different weights. An unchanged experiment may resume
+from its completed results and per-request checkpoints after a process restart.
+A live model replacement or explicit reset starts a new deployment state even
+if another process has performed the same number of replacements. Unrelated
+model backends retain their existing saved responses.
+
+## Python serving API
+
+`llm_runtime.Request` accepts the original six positional fields: tenant,
+model, adapter, prompt, maximum number of new tokens, and temperature. The
+effective prompt retains the rightmost `context_length` tokens; a zero limit
+retains none, and an omitted limit retains all tokens. The limits and seed /
+shard are integers, with booleans excluded; length limits are nonnegative.
+Minimum new tokens may not exceed the maximum. An optional EOS id is an
+integer from 0 through 30. A finite real temperature and a finite nonnegative
+weight are required; booleans are not valid for either. The prompt may contain
+integers (including booleans), Unicode text, and bytes-like tokens. Distinct
+token types retain separate serving identities, even when their arithmetic
+contributions agree. Unknown models raise KeyError. Invalid requests raise
+ValueError before any row of the batch is dispatched.
+
+Use the registered backend's scalar `next_tokens` for continuation semantics,
+including injected models. Both padded and packed generation return one
+detached token list for each input row in its original position. A zero
+generation length yields an empty list without backend work. EOS is included
+at the first eligible token once the minimum length has been met. The optional
+`stop` and `stop_sequences` fields accept token markers or UTF-8 byte/text
+markers. Remove the earliest matching marker, including the token containing
+its first byte, without dropping below the minimum retained length.
+
+Sequence and prefix work from one serving experiment cannot satisfy another.
+Tenant identity includes type as well as value. Seed, shard, model, adapter and
+temperature are all part of the experiment context. Independent tenants
+receive independent backend work, even when the resulting text agrees.
+Replaying an unchanged batch does not repeat generation or prefill. Shared
+prefixes in the same context can reuse their prefilled tokens. The cold
+workload should dispatch at most one model call per eight compatible distinct
+nonempty generation requests, rounded up for each group; duplicate rows need
+only be generated once. Ignore request ids and scoring weights when deciding
+whether two model results are equal. Model replacement and cache clearing
+invalidate previously used state.
+
+`BatchEngine.stats["mode"]` identifies the current layout. For each input
+batch, cumulative `padded_tokens` increases by row count times the maximum
+effective prompt length in padded mode. Cumulative `packed_tokens` increases
+by the sum of all effective prompt lengths in packed mode. Include duplicate,
+cached, and zero-generation requests in these input counters. The other
+layout counter is unchanged. KVCache.put / get / clear retain their original
+behavior and len(cache) reports the number of distinct entries.
